  "hints": [
    "Spread keys over many storage nodes with consistent hashing, and keep several copies of each.",
    "Writes are 40% of 30,000 req/s: size storage for 12,000 writes/s plus cache misses, with 20% headroom.",
    "Router (3) → Coordinators (28) → Redis hot-key cache (2) → NoSQL storage nodes (6)."
  ],
  "scoring": {
    "weights": {
      "performance": 0.35,
      "reliability": 0.3,
      "cost": 0.15,
      "architecture": 0.2
    },
    "latencyTargetMs": 45,
    "costBudget": 3600
  },
  "explanation": [
    "Consistent hashing places keys on a ring so adding a node moves only a small slice of data.",
    "Replicate each key to N nodes and use quorums (for example W=2, R=2 with N=3) to trade consistency against latency.",
    "Hot keys get a small in-memory cache or are split across sub-keys so one partition doesn't melt."
  ]
